[tool_result]1	# Simulation Library CLI Full Reference (`python -m bda`) 2	 3	> Read on demand per the SKILL.md Section 4 guidance. The simulation library package lives in this skill's `scripts/bda/` (pip-editable-installed to this path; `python -m bda` invokes it). 4	 5	## General conventions 6	 7	- Invocation (Bash tool, repo root): `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m bda <subcommand> ...`; all subcommands listed via `-m bda --help` 8	- The parameter bridge is a protocol rule (PyBaMM parameter-name mapping table in SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2); it has no CLI command. 9	- **Must use the Bash tool for simulation and render commands**: the PowerShell tool in this environment is guardrail-limited (`$()` subexpressions, `Set-Location`, `&` multi-operations are all blocked and unapprovable); if only PowerShell is available, the session tool allowlist is abnormal (resume rotation restores it) — retry with Bash first. 10	- JSON is the contract: all inputs/outputs are UTF-8 JSON files; `--out` specifies the output path; each step can be rerun independently. 11	- Same parameters must be reused (spec 5.2 invariant 3): all `run-*` commands check the store cache first, reusing on hit without recomputation. Cache directory = `cache/` under the `--out` file's directory (key = command parameter combination: run-pyamm: params+protocol+base+mode+thermal+plating; run-mlp: smiles+model; run-xtb: smiles; run-orca: smiles+charge+mult+functional; run-md: box+t_ns+engine; run-comp: candidates). Corrupt cache files (invalid JSON / non-object) are treated as misses and rewritten. 12	- Error convention: parameter/validation failures print `bda error: <reason>` to stderr with exit code 1; missing input files or missing JSON keys terminate with a Python traceback — read the last few output lines to locate the cause, fix per the hint, and rerun. 13	- Environment dependencies: `run-xtb` needs the xtb binary on PATH; `run-orca` needs orca on PATH; `run-md` needs gmx on PATH and a corresponding .itp template in the skill's `scripts/bda/simulators/data/opls/`. 14	 15	## Stage 2 funnel judgment (no CLI command) 16	 17	Funnel judgment (hard elimination lines + three-model heterogeneous voting) is executed per protocol rules — see SKILL.md Section 1, Step 1: run `run-mlp --model mace`, `run-mlp --model chgnet`, `run-xtb` for real, in order (same candidate list), then judge directly by reading the three output JSONs. No CLI command, no merged file needed. 18	 19	## run-pyamm — cell simulation 20	 21	``` 22	bda run-pyamm --params PARAMS --protocol PROTOCOL [--base BASE] [--mode MODE] [--thermal THERMAL] [--plating] [--cycles N] --out OUT 23	``` 24	 25	- `--base`: PyBaMM parameter-set name (default `Chen2020`); **the case configuration's `base_params` field must be passed verbatim to `--base`** (e.g., `--base ORegan2022`). Parameter names from the parameter bridge mapping table (SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2) are cross-set shared names (`Electrolyte diffusivity [m2.s-1]`, etc.), so `--params` works directly with any parameter set. 26	- `--protocol` legal values: 27	  - `1C_discharge` (1C discharge, 3600 s, 298.15 K) 28	  - `4C_charge_45C` (4C charge, 900 s, 318.15 K) 29	  - `5C_discharge` (5C high-rate discharge, 720 s — rate scenarios; **high rate recommends `--mode dfn`** — SPMe severely underestimates capacity at 5C) 30	  - `lowT_discharge` (1C discharge, -20 °C/253.15 K — low-temperature scenarios) 31	  - `overcharge` (first 1C discharge to lower cut-off, then 0.5C charge to upper cut-off +0.5 V — overcharge scenarios; output includes T_max_K) 32	  - `aging_1C_100cyc` (100 cycles of 1C constant-current charge/discharge, SEI ec reaction limited + isothermal; voltage limits taken from the parameter set itself) 33	  - `aging_1C_100cyc_45C` (same, but 45 °C/318.15 K high-temperature aging) 34	- `--cycles`: override aging cycle count (default 100) 35	- `--mode`: `spme` (default) / `dfn`; dfn solver failure auto-degrades to SPMe retry (output `model_used` records `"SPMe(fallback)"`) 36	- `--thermal`: `lumped` (default) / `isothermal`; non-isothermal output includes `T_max_K`. The aging protocol internally fixes isothermal; `--thermal`/`--plating` are ignored 37	- `--plating`: enable plating module (Chen2020 parameter set has no plating parameters; standard defaults injected at runtime), output includes `anode_potential_v` 38	- Input `--params`: `{"<PyBaMM parameter name>": value}` — parameter names validated against the chosen parameter set, typically written per the mapping table in SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2 39	- Output keys: `model_used`, `time_s`, `voltage_v`, `capacity_ah`, `T_max_K` (non-isothermal), `anode_potential_v` (--plating); aging protocol outputs `model_used`, `protocol: "aging"`, `cycle_numbers`, `capacity_ah_per_cycle`, `sei_thickness_nm_end` 40	- Errors: 41	  - `unknown protocol 'x'; legal: [...]` → fix protocol name 42	  - `unknown mode 'x'; legal: spme, dfn` → fix mode name 43	  - `unknown parameter name(s): ['...']` → parameter name not in the chosen parameter set; check key names/spelling per the SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2 mapping table 44	  - `base parameter set has no 'SEI kinetic rate constant [m.s-1]'; ...` → chosen system has no aging model (e.g., ORegan2022); aging protocol only on aging-capable sets (Chen2020/OKane2022 etc.); honestly record N/A for systems without aging models 45	  - SPMe solve failure (pybamm.SolverError traceback) → parameter combination invalid; adjust per SKILL.md Section 1, Step 5 fallback 46	- Aging-protocol note: under standard SEI models the capacity trajectory may show a non-monotonic climb-then-saturate artifact (lithium loss shifts the voltage window) — annotate honestly in reports/evaluation, do not treat as normal degradation; coating/doping vs baseline must compare on the same system 47	 48	## run-mlp — ML potential structure relaxation 49	 50	``` 51	bda run-mlp --in IN [--model MODEL] --out OUT 52	``` 53	 54	- `--model`: `mace` (default) / `chgnet` 55	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 56	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "metrics": {"energy_ev": f, "converged": bool}, "model": "mace"}]}` 57	- Errors: `invalid SMILES: '...'` → fix SMILES; `unknown model 'x'; legal: mace, chgnet` → fix model name; `failed to embed 3D structure for ...` → SMILES cannot be conformer-embedded, switch candidate 58	- Where used: Stage 2, once per model (mace and chgnet) 59	 60	## run-xtb — semi-empirical quantum single point 61	 62	``` 63	bda run-xtb --in IN --out OUT 64	``` 65	 66	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 67	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "metrics": {"homo_ev": f, "lumo_ev": f}}]}` 68	- Errors: 69	  - `xtb binary not found; install from https://github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases and put xtb.exe on PATH` → install xtb and add to PATH 70	  - `failed to embed 3D structure for ...` → switch candidate 71	  - `xtb failed: <last 500 chars of stderr>` → troubleshoot per stderr content (structure/convergence issues) 72	  - `failed to parse HOMO/LUMO from xtb output` / `failed to parse total energy from xtb output` → computation ran but output artifact missing; switch conformer or candidate and rerun 73	 74	## run-orca — true DFT endorsement (only closing Top-3) 75	 76	``` 77	bda run-orca --in IN --out OUT 78	``` 79	 80	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 81	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "endorsement": {"E_hartree": f, "homo_ev": f, "lumo_ev": f, "ie_ev": f, "ea_ev": f}}]}` — ie_ev/ea_ev are vertical ionization energy/electron affinity (voltage-window proxies) 82	- Per candidate: gas-phase geometry optimization of neutral/cation/anion three times (r2SCAN-3c + OPT, automatic single point after optimization); spin multiplicity derived from electron count parity per charge state (even→singlet, odd→doublet); max 3 retries per molecule; CPU-slow (~2–3 hours per molecule), only at closing; forbidden inside the funnel 83	- Errors: 84	  - `ORCA binary not found; download academic Windows build from the ORCA forum` → install ORCA and add to PATH 85	  - `ORCA failed after 3 attempts for <smiles> (DFT not converged): ...` → honestly record "this candidate's DFT did not converge"; do not fabricate values 86	 87	## run-md — true MD diffusion endorsement (only closing Top-1) 88	 89	``` 90	bda run-md --box BOX [--engine ENGINE] [--t-ns T_NS] --out OUT 91	``` 92	 93	- Input `--box`: `{"molecules": {"EC": 60, "EMC": 40, "PF6": 10, "Li": 10}}` (Li ≥ 1; `t_ns` may be embedded; `--t-ns` default 10.0) 94	- `--engine`: `gromacs` (default) / `mace`. `mace` = ASE + MACE-MP Langevin NVT (fixed-seed box, 298.15 K, 1 fs step), requires only mace-torch, no GROMACS/.itp templates; for Top-1 cross-validation run both engines and compare D_Li_m2_s. 95	- Output: `{"D_Li_m2_s": f, "trajectory_ok": bool, "drift_check": "ok"|"drift"|"skipped", "achieved_density_g_cm3": f}` — on `trajectory_ok: false` (drift) record and report honestly (mace drift criterion = last-20% mean MACE potential energy drifting > 5% from the middle segment) 96	- Errors: 97	  - `unknown engine 'x'; legal: gromacs, mace` → fix engine name 98	  - `GROMACS not found; install via winget install GROMACS.GROMACS or conda` → install GROMACS (gromacs engine only) 99	  - `mace engine requires mace-torch; install via \`pip install mace-torch\`` → install mace-torch (mace engine only) 100	  - `box must contain at least 1 Li` → box needs ≥ 1 Li 101	  - `missing OPLS-AA .itp template(s): ...` → generate the corresponding .itp templates per the skill's `scripts/bda/simulators/data/opls/README.md` (gromacs engine only) 102	  - `gmx mdrun failed: ...` / `gmx trjconv failed: ...` → troubleshoot per trailing stderr content 103	 104	## render — HTML report 105	 106	``` 107	bda render --case-dir CASE_DIR [--out OUT] 108	``` 109	 110	- Reads `<case_dir>/log.jsonl` (entry 0 criteria + all action entries), produces a self-contained HTML (task overview / iteration trajectory / funnel statistics / stage results / true DFT-MD endorsement / final recommendation / design notes — seven sections), written to `<case_dir>/<out>` (default `report.html`) 111	- No log.jsonl → renders an empty report; no corresponding entry → section shows "no data yet" 112	- Errors: no custom validation; log-line JSON parse failure → traceback pointing at the line number 113	- Where used: last closing step; report content deterministically generated from log.jsonl, no extra LLM calls 114	 115	## run-comp — electrode composition screening (CHGNet periodic relaxation) 116	 117	``` 118	bda run-comp --in IN --out OUT 119	``` 120	 121	- **Environment requirement**: CUDA torch (GPU relaxation ~20 s/state); CPU torch relaxation does not converge (measured). Local `.venv` is CPU torch — use `D:/anaconda/envs/py312/python.exe -m bda run-comp ...` (py312 has chgnet/pymatgen/ase + torch 2.13.0+cu126) 122	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"formula": "Li(Ni0.7Mn0.05Co0.05Si0.1Mg0.1)O2", "name": "NMC-SiMg"}]}` — NMC811 lattice site substitution; TM fractions must sum to 1 123	- Output: `{"baseline": {NMC811 energy + Li metal reference}, "candidates": [{formula, realized_tm_counts, avg_voltage_v, capacity_mah_g, e_full_ev, e_delith_ev, converged, rel_stability_ev_atom}], "calibration_note"}` 124	- Definitions (stated honestly, written to the report): 125	  - Average voltage = −[E(Li_x2)−E(Li_x1)−n_removed·E_Li]/n_removed (x∈[0.3,1], includes Li metal reference; NMC811 self-calibration ≈3.82 vs literature 3.8 V) 126	  - Capacity = 0.7 Li × F/3.6 ÷ molar mass (theoretical proxy; NMC811 ≈194 mAh/g) 127	  - `rel_stability_ev_atom` is for within-batch relative ranking only (relaxation not strictly converged; energy difference for the same composition between two relaxations can be ~1 eV/atom) 128	  - `converged=false` is common (300-step FIRE with fmax 0.1 not reached) — energy at screening precision; annotate honestly 129	  - True endorsement: `run-qe` at closing (periodic DFT, next section) — inside the funnel it is ALWAYS the CHGNet proxy definition 130	- Errors: `TM fractions must sum to 1` → fix composition; `no transition-metal species` → formula lacks TM 131	 132	## run-qe — periodic DFT true endorsement (only closing Top composition) 133	 134	``` 135	bda run-qe --in IN --out OUT 136	``` 137	 138	- **Environment**: MSYS2's QE (native Windows, not a VM): `winget install MSYS2.MSYS2`, switch pacman mirror (TUNA, see install notes), `pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-quantum-espresso`; pw.exe at `C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin\`; pseudopotentials from conda-forge `sssp` package directory (`D:\anaconda\envs\py312\share\sssp\efficiency`, override with env var `QE_PSEUDO_DIR`) 139	- **Two known pitfalls (already handled on this machine; do not repeat)**: ① MSYS2 stock pw.exe reserves only 2 MB stack — initialization stack-overflows (0xC00000FD) — needs pefile patching to `pw_stack4g.exe` (4 GB stack reserve); the runner auto-prefers it; ② backslash is an escape character in Fortran namelists — the runner auto-converts Windows paths to forward slashes when generating input 140	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"formula": "Li(Ni0.8Mn0.1Co0.1)O2", "name": "NMC811"}]}` 141	- Output: per candidate `{formula, realized_tm_counts, avg_voltage_v, e_full_ev, e_delith_ev, e_li_metal_ev, converged, wall_time_s}` — voltage formula same as run-comp (includes Li metal reference) 142	- Computational definitions: ecutwfc 50 Ry / ecutrho 400 (SSSP efficiency standard); nspin=2 ferromagnetic guess (Ni/Mn/Co); lithiated vc-relax + delithiated fixed-cell relax + bcc Li vc-relax; CPU hours (12-atom primitive cell ~1 h/state, 48-atom supercell overnight) — **closing only, forbidden inside the funnel** (same iron rule as run-orca) 143	- Errors: 144	  - `pw.x not found; install MSYS2 ...` → install the MSYS2 quantum-espresso package per guidance 145	  - `QE pseudopotential dir not found; ...` → install conda-forge sssp package or set QE_PSEUDO_DIR 146	  - `no SSSP efficiency pseudopotential entry